Display_Position_Pointers writes each top-three car index to
[ebp+rank*4-0x30] at 0x430149. The original rank slots at -0x30,
-0x2c and -0x28 form one block; the final slot overlaps the vector
whose x/y/z shorts are assigned at -0x28/-0x26/-0x24 before projection
(0x43017c/0x430193/0x4301b9). The initial copies at 0x4300bd..cf
supply the four DWORDs from 0x42e13c/140/130/134. Ghidra split this
block into scalars, so (&iStack_34)[1] and [2] overwrite unrelated
locals and fail ASan on a real championship race start. Preserve the
contiguous rank/vector block and its original overlap, not just its size.

